@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' purpose: how a target is resolved to an image and provisioned before a run can start
' covers: cmd/proveo/provision.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/wizard.go
' covers: cmd/proveo-dev/maintain.go (loadMaintainRegistry, maintainerDefsDir)
' covers: internal/imagebuild/targets.go (BuildTarget, TargetRef, Specs)
'
' ── `proveo targets` IS GONE (N9, DONE (wt) 2026-10-18) ─────────────────────
' MEASURED: cmd/proveo/targets.go is deleted. Nothing in mise.toml, cmd/proveo-dev,
' scripts or tests called the command it registered. maintainerDefsDir
' (PROVEO_DEFS_DIR, else <repo>/defs) moved unchanged into maintain_cmd.go, and
' build, deploy and test read the registry through loadMaintainRegistry. `build`
' was visible in root help; deploy and test stay hidden (usage.puml).
' 2026-10-20: `build` is Hidden again — mise owns the verb — and the command
' remains, so the "missing image" error and the agent-pin line can still name
' `proveo build`. Root help does not list it.
' 2026-10-28: the command left the consumer CLI (usage.puml). maintain_cmd.go is
' cmd/proveo-dev/maintain.go; maintainerDefsDir = PROVEO_DEFS_DIR, else
' proveo-dev repoRoot()/defs. The declined-preflight error names
' PROVEO_AUTO_PROVISION=1; the agent-pin line names `mise run build <target>`.
' KNOWN LIMITS (review, recorded, not fixed; MEASURED):
'   * run.go:229's `proveo build <target>` hint works only inside a source
'     checkout; a binary-only install has no defs/ tree to build from.
'   * provision.go sourceDefsDir and maintain_cmd.go maintainerDefsDir are
'     near-copies with different existence probes: the first requires
'     <root>/defs/base/Dockerfile and returns "" without it; the second accepts
'     any <root>/defs directory and errors without one.
' PROVEO_AUTO_PROVISION goes through envflag (_spec/internal/envflag/
' env-switches.puml): ON builds, OFF declines, anything else asks on a TTY
' with the wizard on.
' HISTORY: `proveo-dev debug` (host-shell-to-go P4) read the registry in-process
' via manifest.Load + maintain.Registry and launched `proveo run <target> --shell`.
' RETIRED 2026-10-17 (the user: "Retire debug too"): cmd/proveo-dev/debug.go,
' its test and `mise run debug` are deleted (MEASURED), and `--shell` with them.
' A shell in a run's sandbox is sbx's: `sbx ls`, then `sbx exec -it <sandbox> bash`.
' Destination diagram — prose from cmd/proveo/{provision,wizard}.go (and the
' deleted targets.go) lands here. Image lineage itself: _spec/_devops/image-lineage-and-publish.puml.
'
' PREFLIGHT, MEASURED: Deps.PreflightImages(man, agentImage) ensures the agent
' image only; run.launchSandbox calls it only off `--print` and only when sbx
' holds no template for the image (!sbx.HasTemplate). No sidecar images remain.
title Preflight provisioning, the maintainer registry, and the missing-env wizard

node "Consumer path — before any container exists" as PRE <<host>> {
  component "preflightImages(manifest, agentImage)\nthe agent image only\n→ the agent image it settled on" as PF <<app>>
  component "provisioner.Ensure([]imageDep)\npull, then a confirmed local build\n→ built: image → ref" as ENS <<app>>
  component "provisionConfirm\nPROVEO_AUTO_PROVISION · else ask on a TTY" as CONF <<app>>
  component "sourceDefsDir\nPROVEO_DEFS_DIR · else the checkout" as SRC <<app>>
  component "buildTarget(defs, manifest, image)\nimagebuild.Specs by image name, else manifest name" as BSH <<app>>
  component "imagebuild.BuildTarget(target, buildTag(image))\nasked :latest → builds :local" as IB <<app>>
}

node "Maintainer path — source tree required" as MAINT <<host>> {
  component "loadMaintainRegistry\nproveo-dev build · deploy · test\n(cmd/proveo-dev/maintain.go)" as LMR <<app>>
  component "maintain.Registry\nmanifest.Load (proveo-dev debug read it\nuntil 2026-10-17)" as REG <<app>>
}

node "Missing declared env" as WIZ <<host>> {
  component "agentio.WizardEnabled · IsStdinTTY" as WEN <<app>>
  component "promptEnv(target, missing)\nEnter skips" as PENV <<app>>
  component "termSecret\nread with echo off" as SEC <<app>>
}

cloud "Docker Hub — proveo/*" as HUB <<cloud>>
component "Agent image present\n(no sidecar images since 2026-10-16)" as READY <<app>>
component "Non-interactive run\nnever prompts, warns and continues" as HEADLESS <<error>>
component "Missing image discovered\nafter the network is up" as LATE <<error>>

PF ARROW_MAIN ENS
ENS ARROW_CLOUD HUB : pull first — the consumer path
ENS ARROW_OPTIONAL CONF : pull failed and a source tree exists
CONF ARROW_MAIN SRC
SRC ARROW_MAIN BSH
BSH ARROW_MAIN IB : in-process, no host bash
IB ARROW_MAIN PF : agent image → the :local ref
LMR ARROW_MAIN REG : same registry, in-process
ENS ARROW_MAIN READY
PF ARROW_ERROR LATE : what running the preflight first prevents
WEN ARROW_MAIN PENV
PENV ARROW_MAIN SEC
WEN ARROW_ERROR HEADLESS
note bottom of REG
  **Maintainer tooling owns no copy of what targets exist.**
  ""manifest.Load"" + ""maintain.Registry"" on ""PROVEO_DEFS_DIR"" (else
  ""<repo>/defs"") is the one registry; build, deploy and test read it through
  ""loadMaintainRegistry"". It replaced ""lib/registry.sh"", which parsed a TSV
  into parallel bash arrays (host-shell-to-go P4). ""proveo targets"", which
  printed that TSV, had no caller and went 2026-10-18 (N9).

  //HISTORY: ""proveo-dev debug"" read the same registry and ran the first//
  //""proveo"" in ""$(go env GOPATH)/bin"" ahead of PATH, so a stale binary could//
  //not report a registry that no longer matched the source. It was retired//
  //2026-10-17 ("Retire debug too") with ""--shell"".//
end note


note bottom of ENS
  **The preflight installs rather than only failing fast**, in dependency
  order, before any network or container exists. The distribution model is
  what makes that the right default: ""mise build"" builds the ""proveo/*""
  images locally, ""mise deploy"" pushes them, and consumers **pull** — so a
  missing image is far more likely to be un-pulled than un-built.

  A build is only offered when a pull fails **and** a source tree is
  present. ""PROVEO_AUTO_PROVISION"" forces the answer either way; on a TTY
  it asks, defaulting to yes — declining just reproduces the failure the
  prompt exists to avoid. The source tree is ""PROVEO_DEFS_DIR"" for dev
  iteration, else the enclosing checkout when it actually carries the build
  sources (""defs/base/Dockerfile"" is the probe; it was the deleted
  ""defs/sidecars/egress-proxy/Dockerfile"" until 2026-10-16); no tree
  means pull-only.

  Mapping an image to its imagebuild target (""buildTarget"") tries the
  image's own name in ""imagebuild.Specs"" first, then the manifest name —
  which covers images whose name differs from their def directory.
end note

note bottom of IB
  **A fallback build never writes "":latest"".** Until 2026-09-22 this path
  ran ""bash <def>/build.sh"" with no arguments: host bash (macOS 3.2), and a
  default ref of "":latest"", which the build refuses for ""--load"" — so the
  end-user fallback could not succeed. ""buildTag"" now maps an asked-for
  "":latest"" to "":local"" (any other tag passes through), and
  ""preflightImages"" hands the run the ref it actually built, which
  ""ResolveImage"" also prefers. A SIDECAR built this way fails the run with
  "re-run so the egress plan picks it up", because the plan already named
  the image it could not pull (_spec/_refactors/host-shell-to-go.puml, P2).
end note

note bottom of WEN
  **The wizard follows the shape the DinD prompt established**: detect the
  need, honour an env short-circuit, prompt only on a TTY, default to the
  safe path. That prompt is gone with its sidecar
  (_spec/_paradigms/retire-dind.puml); the shape it proved is what survives. Only an explicit yes is a yes; ""Enter"" skips a variable and a
  skipped variable stays missing, so the caller still warns about it —
  identical to non-interactive behaviour rather than a second code path.

  Collected values are set in the proveo **process** env, which is what
  lets provider detection and the broker see a key typed at the prompt.
end note


@enduml
